{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1463817822,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDY2Nzg5MTk3NA=="},"added":["conference agenda item"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1463817901,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMDc2NTA0Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/453#issuecomment-220765043"},"message":"Makes it harder to debug #258...","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1463818283,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMDc2NTI5NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/453#issuecomment-220765295"},"message":"Captain's log: GitPython may be more clever than the cmdline:\n\n```\n% datalad install -s http://psydata.ovgu.de/studyforrest/templatetransforms                   \n% cd templatetransforms\n# in the crippled beast\n% git submodule status\nfatal: /usr/lib/git-core/git-submodule cannot be used without a working tree.\n% ipython\nPython 2.7.11+ (default, Mar 23 2016, 11:35:56) \nType \"copyright\", \"credits\" or \"license\" for more information.\n\nIPython 2.4.1 -- An enhanced Interactive Python.\n?         -\u003e Introduction and overview of IPython's features.\n%quickref -\u003e Quick reference.\nhelp      -\u003e Python's own help system.\nobject?   -\u003e Details about 'object', use 'object??' for extra details.\n\nIn [1]: import datalad.api as da\n\nIn [2]: ds=da.Dataset('.')\n\nIn [3]: ds.get_dataset_handles()\nOut[3]: [u'raw/phase2', u'code/ofhelpers', u'raw/structural', u'raw/phase1']\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1463824033,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMDc2ODkxMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/453#issuecomment-220768910"},"message":"Sadly, not:\n\n```\nIn [6]: sm\nOut[6]: git.Submodule(name=raw/structural, path=raw/structural, url=../structural, branch_path=refs/heads/master)\nIn [13]: sm.add(ds.repo.repo, 'raw/structural', 'raw/structural')\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInvalidGitRepositoryError                 Traceback (most recent call last)\n\u003cipython-input-13-563f802eb6fe\u003e in \u003cmodule\u003e()\n----\u003e 1 sm.add(ds.repo.repo, 'raw/structural', 'raw/structural')\n\n/usr/lib/python2.7/dist-packages/git/objects/submodule/base.pyc in add(cls, repo, name, path, url, branch, no_checkout)\n    331             update fails for instance\"\"\"\n    332         if repo.bare:\n--\u003e 333             raise InvalidGitRepositoryError(\"Cannot add submodules to bare repositories\")\n    334         # END handle bare repos\n    335 \n\nInvalidGitRepositoryError: Cannot add submodules to bare repositories\n```\n\nLooks like some soul searching is required.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1463824796,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMDc2OTQzOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/453#issuecomment-220769439"},"message":"Captian's log:\n\n`git --git-dir=.git --work-tree=. status` is a muuuch faster in a direct mode repo than `git annex proxy -- git status` and seems to accomplish the same.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1463825849,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMDc3MDA5MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/453#issuecomment-220770091"},"message":"Lovely:\n\n```\n% git --git-dir=.git --work-tree=. submodule update  raw/structural\nCloning into 'raw/structural'...\nChecking connectivity... done.\nSubmodule path 'raw/structural': checked out '54e555acea857acdb2a8b713cc4c7c7b09607b3d'\n% git --git-dir=.git --work-tree=. status\nOn branch annex/direct/master\nnothing to commit, working directory clean\n% git --git-dir=.git --work-tree=. submodule status             \n-bb29cf28a5e25b9e97a0bb0a97a2eddef46d8a7f code/ofhelpers\n-b2b9d3e73712def6600c5980bdc52535ca613169 raw/phase1\n-ddf2eae956fb782e127321fd913e8a951349e1d3 raw/phase2\n 54e555acea857acdb2a8b713cc4c7c7b09607b3d raw/structural (heads/master)\n```\n\nWorth noting that `.git` in the annex-initted submodule looks like this:\n\n```\ngitdir: /media/mih/USB DISK/templatetransforms/.git/modules/raw/structural\n```\n\nand that annex operations seem to work as expected.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1463826474,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMDc3MDQ3NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/453#issuecomment-220770474"},"message":"And here comes the relief:\n\n```\n% git clone http://psydata.ovgu.de/studyforrest/templatetransforms/.git\nCloning into 'templatetransforms'...\nChecking connectivity... done.\nChecking out files: 100% (924/924), done.\n% cd templatetransforms\n% git annex init\ninit  \n  Detected a filesystem without fifo support.\n\n  Disabling ssh connection caching.\n\n  Detected a crippled filesystem.\n(merging origin/git-annex into git-annex...)\n(recording state in git...)\n\n  Enabling direct mode.\nok\n(recording state in git...)\n% cd raw/structural\n% git clone http://psydata.ovgu.de/studyforrest/structural/.git .   \nCloning into '.'...\nChecking connectivity... done.\n% git annex init\ninit  \n  Detected a filesystem without fifo support.\n\n  Disabling ssh connection caching.\n\n  Detected a crippled filesystem.\n(merging origin/git-annex into git-annex...)\n(recording state in git...)\n\n  Enabling direct mode.\nok\n(recording state in git...)\n% cd ../..\n% git --git-dir=.git --work-tree=. submodule                                    \n-bb29cf28a5e25b9e97a0bb0a97a2eddef46d8a7f code/ofhelpers\n-b2b9d3e73712def6600c5980bdc52535ca613169 raw/phase1\n-ddf2eae956fb782e127321fd913e8a951349e1d3 raw/phase2\n-54e555acea857acdb2a8b713cc4c7c7b09607b3d raw/structural\n% git --git-dir=.git --work-tree=. submodule update --init raw/structural \nSubmodule 'raw/structural' (http://psydata.ovgu.de/studyforrest/templatetransforms/structural) registered for path 'raw/structural'\n% git --git-dir=.git --work-tree=. submodule status                             \n-bb29cf28a5e25b9e97a0bb0a97a2eddef46d8a7f code/ofhelpers\n-b2b9d3e73712def6600c5980bdc52535ca613169 raw/phase1\n-ddf2eae956fb782e127321fd913e8a951349e1d3 raw/phase2\n 54e555acea857acdb2a8b713cc4c7c7b09607b3d raw/structural (heads/annex/direct/master)\n```\n\nNoteably, `raw/structural/.git` is not moved, and not replaced by a file, but is the usual .git directory.\n\nBottom line: all good.\n\nWe should probably adjust the code so that all Git calls and GitPython operations are explicitly configured with the `--git-dir=` and `--work-tree=` equivalent -- regardless of whether we operate on direct or indirect mode repositories.\n\nQuestion: Should we standardize our setup so that submodule `.git` stays in the submodule? Or would there be any negative effects?","files":null},{"type":2,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1463826494,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50NjY3OTE2OTk2"},"title":"git annex direct mode vs. submodule -\u003e dead end? Doesn't look like it!","was":"git annex direct mode vs. submodule -\u003e dead end? Doesn't look like it!"},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1463883970,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMDgxMDc3Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/453#issuecomment-220810776"},"message":"@joeyh please pardon my ignorant question, but why https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/453#issuecomment-220769439 ?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1463936526,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMDg0MzQwNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/453#issuecomment-220843404"},"message":"I don't think it's safe at all to use --work-tree in direct mode repositories. Any git command that actually manipulates the work tree could overwrite/delete the annex files with the symlinks from the git repository. \n\nThat is basically the same as removing the direct mode guard (configuring the repo to not be considered to be a bare repo), which is there to prevent such foot-shooting deletion of potentially the only copy of a file in a direct mode repository.\n\nv6 mode is a much better solution to this probem.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1463937544,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMDg0NDI5OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/453#issuecomment-220844298"},"message":"Thanks @joeyh !\n\nI will start playing with v6 repos and see how they play alongside submodules.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1463940234,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMDg0NjYyMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/453#issuecomment-220846620"},"message":"I spent some time manually trying out the most essential bits from the datalad PoV with V6 repos. I agree with @joeyh that this is a much better solution. Not just to the handling of submodules, but also to  some of the issues we are still ignoring (AFNI dereferencing files, ...).\n\nI'd suggest that you also take a look, if you haven't yet. We should really consider doing v6 right from the start for datalad's datasets.\n\nDuring the next meeting we should discuss, whether we want to go v6 and whether we want to present \"unlocked\" files by default.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1463944204,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMDg1MDA2MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/453#issuecomment-220850060"},"message":"Note that git annex adjust --unlock makes it easy to switch a repository\nto presenting unlocked files locally while keeping them locked in other\nclones. I could very easily add the --lock to go the other way if there\nis a use case for it.\n\nv6 mode still has some warts though, including speed problems that will\nneed patches to git to resolve. Drop or get some files with git annex\nand run git status to see one of the problems..\n\n(And a big thank you to DataLad/Dartmouth for making v6 development possible!\nIt's rare to be in a position to be able to try out big speculative\nchanges like this.)\n\n## \n\nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1464001774,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMDk1MTYwMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/453#issuecomment-220951600"},"message":"@joeyh Thanks for the information, and thanks for everything else, too!","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1464101886,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIyMTI5ODUzOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/453#issuecomment-221298539"},"message":"for reference: annex page describing outstanding issues with v6/smudge filters: https://git-annex.branchable.com/todo/smudge/","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1480168734,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDg3MjYxMjI3Nw=="},"added":["annex-v6/7"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1497266803,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwNzc2MjgxNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/453#issuecomment-307762815"},"message":"We are doing much better on this topic in current master. Closing.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1497266803,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTExOTI4NTYyNg=="},"status":2}]}